    "narrative": "Our optimal lineup for May 30th leans into high-contact efficiency and favorable matchups against mid-tier arms. **Vinnie Pasquantino** leads the charge with a 69.49 efficiency score, benefiting from a soft matchup against Rocker and a significant +14% boost from the dynamic platoon advantage. Alongside him, **Josh Naylor** (64.20) and **James Wood** (62.98) provide the core stability; **James Wood** is particularly well-positioned as our primary stolen base threat, maintaining a strong xwOBA of 0.384 despite the threat of King on the mound. **Brice Turang** rounds out the elite tier at 60.94, capitalizing on a prime spot in the order against Lambert. While **Corbin Carroll** sits just outside the 60+ threshold at 59.57, his xwOBA of 0.373 remains a focal point of our offensive ceiling, provided he avoids the strikeout volatility often presented by Woo.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Alex Freeland**, whose score of 35.63 failed to crack the starting nine largely due to the intimidating presence of Luzardo. While **Alex Freeland** offers switch-hitting versatility, the -18% penalty for facing an elite left-handed arm proved too deep a hole to climb out of, especially when compared to the favorable park factors currently lifting **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Kyle Karros**. We are also keeping a cautious eye on our \"Lineup Pending\" designations; **Gabriel Moreno**, **Kyle Karros**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Tyler Soderstrom** all carry elevated risk profiles today. Should these players shift lower in the batting order once official lineups are posted, their efficiency scores will adjust downward, potentially pushing them toward our substitution floor. With **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are effectively managing our limited roster depth while waiting for the return of impact pieces like **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, and **Henry Bolte** to restore our full competitive capacity.",
